- **Physics Solved:**  
  - Elastic-plastic structural behavior under combined loading (bending, shear, and axial stresses); nonlinear material response including yield initiation and plastic zone propagation.  

- **Target Outputs (Metrics):**  
  - Von-Mises equivalent stress distribution (Figs. 3–6);  
  - Vertical displacement (Y-direction) at mid-span (Fig. 7);  
  - Shear stress distribution near beam ends (Fig. 8);  
  - Plastic zone expansion (red regions in stress clouds);  
  - Critical load threshold for yield initiation (observed at ~30 kN).  

- **Optimization Goal:**  
  - Strengthen structural bearing capacity by identifying and reinforcing weak sections (e.g., hole perimeters and shear-critical end regions) to delay plastic collapse and reduce stress concentration.

10_1016_j_eml_2025_102339.key_3:
- **Physics Solved:** Mechanical stress distribution in polymer-encapsulated electronic components under hydrostatic pressure; Stress concentration phenomena around rigid inclusions in a soft matrix
- **Target Outputs (Metrics):** Maximum shear stress; Average shear stress; Shear stress concentration factor (ratio of maximum shear stress to external hydrostatic pressure); Geometric coherence index (κ); Objective function J = min{max[κij|(i≠j)] + avg[κij|(i≠j)]}
- **Optimization Goal:** Minimize both maximum and average shear stress on circuit boards by optimizing component arrangement; Achieve up to 45.5% reduction in shear stress; Prevent solder joint failure through stress concentration reduction

